e, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 10340400, "full_name": "Alexander Mraz", "first_name": "Alexander", "last_name": "Mraz", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 10340397, "full_name": "Takehiro Kashiyama", "first_name": "Takehiro", "last_name": "Kashiyama", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/RDD2022_-_The_multi-national_Road_Damage_Dataset_released_through_CRDDC_2022/21431547", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<h2>Description</h2>\n<ol>\n  <li>The Road Damage Dataset, RDD2022, is released as a part of the Crowdsensing-based Road Damage Detection Challenge (CRDDC'2022), an IEEE BigData Cup.\u00a0</li>\n  <li>It comprises <strong>47,420 road images</strong> from six countries, <strong>Japan, India, the Czech Republic, Norway, the United States, and China.\u00a0</strong></li>\n  <li>The images have been annotated with more than <strong>55,000</strong> instances of road damage.\u00a0</li>\n  <li>Four types of road damage, namely longitudinal cracks, transverse cracks, alligator cracks, and potholes, are captured in the dataset.\u00a0</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Usage</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li>The annotated dataset is envisioned for developing <strong>deep learning</strong>-based methods to detect and classify road damage <strong>automatically.\u00a0</strong></li>\n  <li>The <strong>municipalities and road agencies </strong>may utilize the RDD2022 dataset, and the models trained using RDD2022 for low-cost automatic monitoring of road conditions.\u00a0</li>\n  <li>Further,<strong> computer vision and machine learning researchers </strong>may use the dataset to benchmark the performance of different algorithms for other image-based applications of the same type (classification, object detection, etc.).\u00a0</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For further details, please refer to the CRDDC'2022 resources.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 13267424441, "created_date": "2022-10-29T10:53:29Z", "modified_date": "2023-05-30T10:01:26Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Road damages", "Damage detection.", "Condition monitoring", "deep learning dataset", "Deep Learning Applications", "Artificial Intelligence", "automation", "Computer Vision", "Computer Graphics", "Applied Computer Science", "Computer Engineering", "Infrastructure Engineering and Asset Management", "Geospatial Information Systems", "Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing", "Transport Engineering"], "keywords": ["Road damages", "Damage detection.", "Condition monitoring", "deep learning dataset", "Deep Learning Applications", "Artificial Intelligence", "automation", "Computer Vision", "Computer Graphics", "Applied Computer Science", "Computer Engineering", "Infrastructure Engineering and Asset Management", "Geospatial Information Systems", "Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing", "Transport Engineering"], "categories": [{"id": 28879, "title": "Computer vision", "parent_id": 28867, "path": "/28798/28867/28879", "source_id": "460304", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29014, "title": "Computer graphics", "parent_id": 29008, "path": "/28798/29008/29014", "source_id": "460702", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 28822, "title": "Applied computing not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 28801, "path": "/28798/28801/28822", "source_id": "460199", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 26494, "title": "Digital processor architectures", "parent_id": 26485, "path": "/26212/26485/26494", "source_id": "400903", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 29236, "title": "Other information and computing sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_id": 29233, "path": "/28798/29233/29236", "source_id": "469999", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 26365, "title": "Infrastructure engineering and asse